# Fail closed.
#
# This working tree holds RAW operational documents (device identifiers, build
# fingerprints, credential paths, security posture). The remote is a PUBLIC
# GitHub repository. Nothing here is publishable unless it has been sanitized.
#
# Therefore: ignore everything by default, and allow ONLY an explicit list.
# A stray `git add .` must never be able to stage a raw document.

*

# --- explicitly publishable ---
!.gitignore
!README.md
!SANITIZED_*.md

# Note: files already tracked stay tracked regardless of this file, and
# `git add -f` still overrides it. Neither should be used on a raw document.
